{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2861af9a73966356710244eddb70a4f66935eca474db9f6aff03cfaf8fe6acc5","digest":{"component_or_area":"opcert_service/app worker lifecycle","key_entities":["src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py","tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted","tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_worker_cancellation_survives_job_completion_race","_worker","asyncio.timeout","asyncio.to_thread","lifespan","queue.get()"],"problem_keywords":["asyncio.wait_for","cancellation race","Python 3.11","xdist worker crash","lifespan teardown","CPython issue 86296"],"propositions":["Python 3.11 asyncio.wait_for consumes external worker cancellation when its child completes in the same turn (CPython issue 86296), leaving the worker with cancelling()>0 and stuck at queue.get() while lifespan awaits forever.","TestClient teardown triggers lifespan cancellation that collides with job completion, causing the hang guard timeout to kill the xdist worker after test_matching_guard_is_accepted.","Replacing asyncio.wait_for with asyncio.timeout semantics (matching Python 3.12 behavior) preserves external cancellation and allows prompt worker termination when shutdown collides with job completion.","The opcert worker must terminate promptly on external cancellation even when job completion races with shutdown, while preserving per-job timeout semantics and 202 ACK behavior."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787775975928838001,"uuid":"a20e0033-a9e4-4cba-b83e-9711dec0c660"}